---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import config from "../../site.config.mjs";
---
<Base title="Privacy notice" description={`${config.brandName} Privacy notice (draft for legal review).`}>
  <PageHead title="Privacy notice" lead="Draft for legal review. This page is a template and is not yet in force." />
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="legal">
      <p class="tag">Draft for legal review</p>
      <p>Who we are, what personal data the website and sandbox collect (contact details you send us, request logs kept for 30 days), why, how long we keep it, who processes it for us, and your rights under UK and EU data protection law. The website is hosted on Vercel, which keeps visitor IP addresses in its server logs; the final notice will state for how long.</p>
      <p><strong>Until then, what the access form does.</strong> If you send the access form, we store your name, work email, job title, company, country of incorporation and your answers, and use them only to reply and arrange a call. They are stored on our application servers in the EU (Frankfurt). We don’t sell them, use them for advertising or add you to a mailing list. The status page asks our application server for its health from your browser, which shows that server your IP address.</p>
      <p><strong>Your rights.</strong> You can ask to see, correct or delete what you sent us by writing to <a class="textlink" href={`mailto:${config.salesInbox}`}>{config.salesInbox}</a>. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ico.org.uk).</p>
      <p class="soft">The final text will be published after legal review, before the sandbox opens.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal { max-width: 64ch; display: grid; gap: 18px; font-size: 18px; }
  .tag { justify-self: start; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--wait) 12%, transparent); color: var(--wait); border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 12px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }
</style>
